  (c) NO RELATION: DE1-DE13 use a constant Lambda background (E^2 = Om(1+z)^3 + 1 - Om) and read Omega_L as a threshold; DE7 found the gate ill-posed when varied as an action term; no equation for rho_DE(t)
  (d) BOUNDS (derived inequality, not a forcing): class A is one-sided (CFG541 open item 5), so if a0 falls after a system settles the cold energy overfills (rho_c > rho_ph) and is never removed. Then a settled galaxy's dynamical a0 = max of a0(t) since it settled. Under the framework's own prediction (Lambda + trickle, rho_DE non-decreasing) the ratchet never binds. If rho_DE falls (w > -1), local galaxies read the past maximum: kappa_fit = kappa_true sqrt(rho_max/rho_0); the size under DESI is evaluated at the test stage

